Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: kasi the threat na itanggal sila sa TES,

4513
04:19:04,340 --> 04:19:06,380
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: kasi hindi nila masyadong naiintindihan eh.

4514
04:19:06,580 --> 04:19:09,060
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: Akala nila it was the school giving the TES,

4515
04:19:09,360 --> 04:19:11,860
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: dahil kontrolado ng school yung pondo.

4516
04:19:12,200 --> 04:19:13,880
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: By the time they received their money,

4517
04:19:13,880 --> 04:19:15,300
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: all the deduction,

4518
04:19:15,560 --> 04:19:16,320
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: diba?

4519
04:19:16,820 --> 04:19:19,180
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: Minsan solo, na isang eskwelahan,

4520
04:19:19,340 --> 04:19:20,800
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: lahat kanila yun,

4521
04:19:20,800 --> 04:19:22,540
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: pero sa kanila na pupunta.

4522
04:19:22,720 --> 04:19:25,780
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: So it's so unfair to the students,

4523
04:19:25,780 --> 04:19:28,260
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: dahil ayaw nilang magreklamo,

4524
04:19:28,260 --> 04:19:30,400
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: dahil baka matanggal sila.

4525
04:19:30,910 --> 04:19:51,320
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: So I'm glad that finally na nagagawa na ito and of course giving justice to the deserving students na sila ang magdideside kung ano ang deduction na ibabawas sa kanila nung eskwelahan dahil sila na mismo ang humahawak ng pondo.

4526
04:19:51,380 --> 04:19:55,240
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: Again, maraming salamat Ched for introducing this reform.

4527
04:19:55,520 --> 04:19:56,060
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: Thank you.

4528
04:19:56,140 --> 04:19:56,760
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Thank you po.

4529
04:19:58,220 --> 04:20:02,260
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: About 80% na ang na-distributan po.

4530
04:20:02,320 --> 04:20:04,320
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: About 700,000 plus.

4531
04:20:05,140 --> 04:20:06,160
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ayan, exact.

4532
04:20:06,400 --> 04:20:07,700
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Real time po kasi ito.

4533
04:20:07,900 --> 04:20:11,220
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We have a real time digital system with land bank.

4534
04:20:11,300 --> 04:20:12,500
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So as of this time,

4535
04:20:12,740 --> 04:20:19,920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 3.30, meron ng 722,751 students.

4536
04:20:20,300 --> 04:20:26,320
Senior Deputy Speaker Ferdinand L. Hernandez: And congratulations, Chair, kasi kalmado ka na ngayon.

4537
04:20:28,180 --> 04:20:28,740
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: All right.

4538
04:20:29,440 --> 04:20:31,560
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes, the Honorable, please continue.

4539
04:20:31,560 --> 04:20:32,960
Rep. Brian Poe: Thank you, Madam Chair.

4540
04:20:33,180 --> 04:20:43,620
Rep. Brian Poe: I wanted to highlight that because you said you addressed 80% of the backlog of our scholars and we have how many again, 700 something thousand?

4541
04:20:44,520 --> 04:20:45,880
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 722,000.

4542
04:20:45,880 --> 04:20:47,860
Rep. Brian Poe: out of 900 plus thousand.

4543
04:20:47,880 --> 04:20:54,200
Rep. Brian Poe: So that's 722,000 students who now have bank accounts with zero maintaining balance.

4544
04:20:54,400 --> 04:20:54,760
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

4545
04:20:54,840 --> 04:20:57,740
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Chair, this addresses two problems immediately.

4546
04:20:57,740 --> 04:21:03,520
Rep. Brian Poe: One is the efficiency of government scholarships and the second is financial literacy.

4547
04:21:03,920 --> 04:21:11,260
Rep. Brian Poe: You are immediately teaching students how to open a bank account, how to save money and how to maintain a bank account.

4548
04:21:11,440 --> 04:21:13,300
Rep. Brian Poe: We are banking the unbanked.

4549
04:21:13,300 --> 04:21:18,060
Rep. Brian Poe: We're creating another generation of students who now know how to save money.

4550
04:21:18,680 --> 04:21:25,140
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Chair, this is a very important step forward for Ched and I believe we should continue to support it.

4551
04:21:25,140 --> 04:21:38,360
Rep. Brian Poe: I also saw that in your budget, you have a 214% increase, I believe, or sorry, a 150% increase in the budget for the Bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship.

4552
04:21:38,360 --> 04:21:38,820
Rep. Brian Poe: Is this correct?

4553
