CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

4554
04:21:43,540 --> 04:21:46,100
Rep. Brian Poe: Can you tell me a little bit about this program?

4555
04:21:46,240 --> 04:21:50,120
Rep. Brian Poe: I believe, obviously, it's for our merit scholars, our top performing students.

4556
04:21:50,480 --> 04:21:52,660
Rep. Brian Poe: How many students are supported by this program?

4557
04:21:53,680 --> 04:21:54,200
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah.

4558
04:21:54,280 --> 04:21:55,100
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Thank you very much.

4559
04:21:55,220 --> 04:22:00,500
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Foremost, I would like to credit His Excellency, our President, kasi tinanong niya noon.

4560
04:22:00,800 --> 04:22:03,040
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kasi I really am very thankful.

4561
04:22:03,220 --> 04:22:15,240
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Sabi niya, bakit ang dami nating, ang EDCOM release na madaming programs na hindi tine-take ng mga estudyante.

4562
04:22:15,460 --> 04:22:17,020
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Bakit ang daming attrition?

4563
04:22:17,380 --> 04:22:18,540
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: That was the question.

4564
04:22:18,680 --> 04:22:20,000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So we came up with the proposal.

4565
04:22:20,380 --> 04:22:23,480
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: The proposal caters the top five

4566
04:22:23,480 --> 04:22:33,140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Graduates of senior high school who are willing first to enroll to the ten priority programs identified by EDCOM.

4567
04:22:33,140 --> 04:22:38,420
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Number two, they are accepted to a top performing university.

4568
04:22:38,880 --> 04:22:40,740
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May criteria po eh yung university.

4569
04:22:41,160 --> 04:22:44,120
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Whether state university or private.

4570
04:22:44,560 --> 04:22:50,260
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And the student will receive kung private siya, subsidized.

4571
04:22:50,400 --> 04:22:51,920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Mga 80,000 ba?

4572
04:22:52,000 --> 04:22:53,160
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Can you give me the number?

4573
04:22:53,400 --> 04:22:56,360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kung private siya, 90,000.

4574
04:22:56,760 --> 04:23:02,240
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kung sa government naman, state university, libre kasi ang tuition fee.

4575
04:23:02,240 --> 04:23:11,400
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: In terms of allowance, ang isang estudyante nakaka-receive ng 45,000 per semester.

4576
04:23:11,400 --> 04:23:14,600
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: For academic year.

4577
04:23:17,300 --> 04:23:17,760
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah.

4578
04:23:17,880 --> 04:23:18,920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yun po yung ano.

4579
04:23:19,040 --> 04:23:24,800
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Pero ngayon po, of the 20,000 slots for 2026,

4580
04:23:25,020 --> 04:23:28,000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: sa dami ng magagaling na nag-graduate,

4581
04:23:28,000 --> 04:23:32,680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: we receive already more than 39,000 applicants.

4582
04:23:33,620 --> 04:23:38,880
Rep. Brian Poe: But how do we decide, how do we distribute that, Madam Chair, if I may ask?

4583
04:23:39,380 --> 04:23:41,440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We have a formula developed.

4584
04:23:42,340 --> 04:23:45,040
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We have a formula developed.

4585
04:23:45,320 --> 04:23:51,040
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So wala pong bahid ng irregularities doon.

4586
04:23:51,040 --> 04:23:57,000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kasi may, based on the grade, based on the per capita income of the students,

4587
04:23:57,000 --> 04:24:03,000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: meron ding point yung siya ay first generation in the family.

4588
04:24:03,040 --> 04:24:03,860
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ano pa, Cor?

4589
04:24:05,580 --> 04:24:07,000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And then the...

4590
04:24:14,954 --> 04:24:16,580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

4591
04:24:16,580 --> 04:24:17,420
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

4592
04:24:17,520 --> 04:24:17,900
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

4593
04:24:19,960 --> 04:24:20,660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

4594
04:24:21,480 --> 04:24:28,460
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Proportionately distributed based on the number of graduates of senior high school per region.

4595
04:24:28,460 --> 04:24:30,580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Na nasa top five.

4596
04:24:30,760 --> 04:24:32,340
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May formula po doon.

4597
04:24:32,980 --> 04:24:35,440
Rep. Brian Poe: So it's truly, it's really merit.

4598
04:24:35,640 --> 04:24:38,200
Rep. Brian Poe: So there's no aspect of economics behind it.

4599
04:24:38,320 --> 04:24:38,680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

4600
04:24:38,800 --> 04:24:39,380
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay.

4601
04:24:39,440 --> 04:24:42,280
Rep. Brian Poe: So it doesn't matter if you're considered poorest of the poor.

4602
04:24:42,420 --> 04:24:46,540
Rep. Brian Poe: You don't necessarily have a leg up over someone else.

4603
04:24:46,580 --> 04:24:47,680
Rep. Brian Poe: It's really based on grades.

4604
04:24:48,120 --> 04:24:52,140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Zero to two million at least na household income.

4605
04:24:52,440 --> 04:24:54,180
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Irregular family naman hindi naman.

4606
04:24:54,340 --> 04:24:54,900
Rep. Brian Poe: Ah, okay.

4607
04:24:54,980 --> 04:25:00,760
Rep. Brian Poe: So it's only those with zero to, to two million pesos or one million pesos annual income?

4608
